Daemon requests through the extension host in browser-based IDEs

The webview fetches from the daemon on the loopback of the machine running
the extension host. In a browser-based IDE (Theia, code-server, VS Code for
the Web) the webview runs in the user's browser, where that loopback is the
user's own machine, and nothing forwards the port, so the shell fails with
'Failed to load workspace'. When vscode.env.uiKind is Web, the extension
now sends webShellBootstrap with daemonBridge: true, and the webview routes
every fetch to the daemon's origin as messages to the extension host, which
performs it next to the daemon and streams the response back. Only the
daemon's origin is forwarded; the daemon stays on loopback. Local and
remote desktop windows are unchanged. Features opening their own
WebSockets to the daemon (terminal, live browser, voice, local files) are
not bridged yet.

